      "general": {
        "abstract": "The site is located in the Congo Basin. The region is part of a floristic group identified as semi-deciduous evergreen. Canopy height model (CHM) data indicate the presence of a heterogeneous canopy with an average tree height of 29.3 m and 95% of the identified crowns between 21.2 m and 38.8 m. The CongoFlux research site is located at the Institut National pour l'Etude et la Recherche Agronomique (INERA), Yangambi Centre (CRY) built in the 1930s.",
